From: Victor Momplet <mompletvictor@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 19:25:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?fix:=20audit=20of=20the=20fork's=20own=20featur?=
 =?UTF-8?q?es=20=E2=80=94=20coherent=20figures,=20consent,=20cost=20and=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?Spanish?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Findings of a full audit (code review + the wearer's phone), fixed together:

- Training: deleting, bulk-deleting or re-timing a workout takes its exercise log with it (hooks in
  AppViewModel); a session whose workout is gone stops adding to the day's Effort; a workout logged twice
  counts once; a plan added to a running workout joins its plan instead of replacing it; upstream's silent
  discards drop the live plan too; the row is put back to the session's figures if a rescore reverts it;
  a session analysed with no heart rate is looked at again after 20 samples; a failed analysis is retried
  after an hour, not on every look; a second analysis asked while one runs is run after it.
- Effort: Claude's reference points now sit on the app's own logarithmic 0-100 axis.
- Consent: the workout analysis sends body, resting HR and heart rate, and the weekly review runs at all,
  only with the coach's data consent.
- Cost: weekly review and meal scores back off after a failure; "-1, too little to judge" is kept as an
  answer; a meal logged after its slot waits 20 min for its last photo; cancelling a photo or workout
  analysis now cancels the HTTP call (enqueue + invokeOnCancellation); a double tap on a frequent meal
  logs it once.
- Dates: calendar events stay on their clock hours on the 23/25-hour days (25-10-2026); a meal before
  04:00 belongs to the night before; "My day" follows the date after the night.
- Spanish: the coach replies in the phone's language and calls the scores Carga/Esfuerzo/Descanso, its
  suggestion chips and refusal read in Spanish; sport names on screen in Spanish; no raw English API text
  under errors; an empty Anthropic account is named; decimals with the phone's mark on the Scale card.
- AMOLED: text-field borders and chart grid lines drawn strong enough to see; training mode chips no
  longer break "Sugiéreme" on a 384 dp screen.
- Robustness: a non-JSON Google Tasks reply, a failed write, a partial Health Connect page or a cancelled
  refresh no longer crash, write partial sums or block the next read.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
